Alembic migrations for Segmently.

The database URL is taken from the DATABASE_URL environment variable
(see alembic/env.py), so run migrations with, e.g.:

    cd backend
    export DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/segmently
    alembic upgrade head

To create a new autogenerated revision after changing models:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"

Revision 0001_initial was hand-written (alembic was not installed in the
authoring environment); regenerate/verify it against the models once the
toolchain and a live database are available.
